Fix aggregated potential-ET unit conversion in parallel DHSVM

The DHSVM parallel branch (pnnl/DHSVM-PNNL, branch `parallel`) last synced
with `master` on 2020-09-11.  On 2021-06-10 the serial `master` branch fixed
a unit-conversion bug in Aggregate.c (commit 902bb2a, "Update Aggregate.c")
that the parallel branch never received.

EvapoTranspiration.c computes EPot as a rate in m/s -- its own comment says
so ("Calculate the evaporation rate in m/s"), and the line below it divides
MoistureFlux by Dt.  Converting that rate to a depth over the timestep
requires MULTIPLYING by Dt.  Both branches divided.

In the parallel branch the NPixels normalisation was refactored into the
APPLY_MACRO block, so only the Dt term remains here and the fix is a single
character.  The error is a factor of Dt^2 -- about 1e8 at a 3 h timestep --
which leaves aggregated potential ET around eight orders of magnitude too
small.

The effect is DIAGNOSTIC ONLY: MassBalance.c forms its Output term from
Evap.ETot (actual ET), not EPot, so the simulated water balance is
unaffected.  It corrupts the PotTransp.Story* columns of Aggregated.Values.

Verified on the Lower Connecticut River Basin: before the fix the physical
constraint EPot >= EAct (potential >= actual transpiration) was violated in
46 of 114 timesteps; after the fix it holds in all of them.

Apply with:
    cd <DHSVM-PNNL checkout, branch parallel>
    patch -p1 < dhsvm-parallel-epot-fix.patch

--- a/DHSVM/sourcecode/Aggregate.c
+++ b/DHSVM/sourcecode/Aggregate.c
@@ -352,7 +352,16 @@
   
   for (i = 0; i < Veg->MaxLayers + 1; i++) {
     /* convert EPot from m/s to m */
-    Total->Evap.EPot[i] /= Dt;
+    /* WW-DHSVM: ported from the serial master branch, commit 902bb2a
+       (2021-06-10, "Update Aggregate.c"), which the parallel branch never
+       received -- it last synced with master on 2020-09-11.  Converting a
+       rate in m/s to a depth in m over the timestep requires MULTIPLYING
+       by Dt; the original divided, leaving aggregated potential ET wrong
+       by a factor of Dt^2 (about 1e8 at a 3 h timestep).  Diagnostic only:
+       MassBalance.c uses Evap.ETot, not EPot, so the simulated water
+       balance was never affected.  The NPixels normalisation is applied
+       separately here by the MACRO above, so only the Dt term changes. */
+    Total->Evap.EPot[i] *= Dt;
   }
 
 
